  "giftFurrowLore": "Nothing in the field dies alone. The first cut follows the roots beneath it.",
  "giftAftermathLore": "The harvest remembers what survived. Those touched by the blade remain within its reach.",
  "giftGatheringLore": "One stalk, then another. The hand finds a rhythm that the field cannot close against.",
  "giftPassageLore": "A ferryman promises arrival. Even a furious passenger cannot overturn that promise.",
  "giftAnchorLore": "The crossing has no shore beneath it. The ferryman learns to make a shore of stillness.",
  "giftReturnLightLore": "Every stroke of the pole leaves a little light behind. Enough light can guide a trembling hand home.",
  "giftForeknowledgeLore": "A careful keeper opens the ledger before the dead arrive. The first reading leaves nothing concealed.",
  "giftVerdictLore": "Judgement begins when the room falls silent. Only the right seal can carry the sentence.",
  "giftEquilibriumLore": "Three true measures bring the scales level. For a moment, every debt lies open.",
  "giftFirstLightLore": "The chooser sees a death before anyone else does. The first light is also the first wound.",
  "giftReprisalLore": "A death that reaches for the chooser has chosen itself. The answer arrives on the returning blade.",
  "giftLastWordLore": "A spirit may argue until the end. The chooser saves the last word for what remains.",
  "giftHungerLore": "The empty collar remembers every meal it missed. Silence gives that hunger a head start.",
  "giftEchoLore": "A shriek cannot drown out an absence. Beneath the noise, the old rhythm waits.",
  "giftUnbrokenLore": "There is no head to lose. Even a wandering hand cannot break the chain at once.",
  "giftHushLore": "Before a death is announced, the mourner grants a little silence. Even the dead must wait their turn.",
  "giftKeeningLore": "The mourner listens until the cry has passed. The next toll carries what was heard.",
  "giftRefrainLore": "A bell cannot call a name only once. Each refrain gives the departing soul longer to answer.",
